task: intent-4b-with-more-data
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/intent-4b-with-more-data
worktree: ../okay-wt-4b

why: the entry's prediction — "the 4B embedder is worse at 60
  examples because 2560 dimensions need more of them": re-run the
  learning curve on BOTH embedders and find where the lines cross.
  The gateway has both (Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B at 1024 dims,
  Qwen3-Embedding-4B at 2560), and intent-instruction-prefix just
  measured the bar a single split cannot see past (ten points on
  sixty test messages) — so the curve runs on both mirror splits.

what: TestLearningCurveBoth (Live): each model embeds the 120-row
  fixture once; for each mirror split the training half grows
  class-balanced 8..60; probe and centroid at each n, per model, per
  split, and the two splits' mean; a crossing is reported only if it
  holds on both splits. Conditions on every row. No default moves on
  this alone: it decides which vectoriser a distilled corpus should
  be measured with.
